# shell: desktop
# AW-029: the desk Trash icon speaks for EVERY volume's trash -- a file
# trashed on another volume fills it, and emptying it empties the icon,
# both live on the refresh beat, with the home trash empty throughout.
wait 10
note the empty-trash art at rest
expect-pixel 175 23 336698
write /dev/shm/.Trash/xplant.txt hi
wait 200
note another volume's trash gained a file: the icon fills
expect-pixel 175 23 000000
remove /dev/shm/.Trash/xplant.txt
wait 200
note and empties again when that trash empties
expect-pixel 175 23 336698
quit
